# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first match wins. 301 is used
# throughout because these are permanent canonicalisation redirects, and a 302
# would leave search engines indexing the source URL.
#
# NOT VERIFIED. A _redirects file only takes effect once the apex domain is
# attached to the Pages project and DNS resolves. Until the site is deployed
# these rules are declarative intent, not confirmed behaviour. See the
# owner-action note in the technical SEO report.

# Apex to www. www is the canonical host every canonical URL, hreflang tag and
# sitemap entry names, so the apex must not serve a second copy of the site.
https://easyinvoiceocr.com/* https://www.easyinvoiceocr.com/:splat 301
http://easyinvoiceocr.com/* https://www.easyinvoiceocr.com/:splat 301

# Plain HTTP on the canonical host. Cloudflare's "Always Use HTTPS" setting
# normally handles this at the edge before a request reaches Pages; this is the
# belt-and-braces copy in case that setting is ever off.
http://www.easyinvoiceocr.com/* https://www.easyinvoiceocr.com/:splat 301
